{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_28_flowchart_model_ladder_lift_plan", "label": "Flowchart Model-Ladder Lift plan (NOT PURSUED)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-28-flowchart-model-ladder-lift.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stopped before Task 1 because its own controls shrank it to nothing: sealing escaping-hostile as held-out leaves exactly one discovery cell, and the outcome space ('sonnet saturates' or 'haiku gains a point on one task') changes no decision."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_28_flowchart_model_ladder_lift_paired_matrix_rule", "label": "The matrix is always paired \u2014 report the lift, never the raw score", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-28-flowchart-model-ladder-lift.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An absolute score is not admissible evidence \u2014 a model may pass without the skill entirely. Every model runs {with skill} x {without skill}, identical except for --skill, and the measured quantity is the lift. Cheap to hold, and the one thing arena structurally cannot express."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_28_flowchart_model_ladder_lift_null_skill_control", "label": "Null-skill control as the admissibility fork", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-28-flowchart-model-ladder-lift.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If the reference model saturates the task without the skill, the task measures the model and is a regression guard rather than an improvement instrument \u2014 nothing downstream is worth running until that is known."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_28_flowchart_model_ladder_lift_e2b_capability_floor", "label": "e2b capability-floor finding (Task 0)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-28-flowchart-model-ladder-lift.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "176 byte-identical Skill calls, zero Write/Edit/Read/Bash: the model got the full SKILL.md, embedded the output path in its own args every time, and never called Write. It read Skill's terse ack as failure and retried until it concluded the tool was broken. A capability defect no SKILL.md wording reaches \u2014 and it disproves the context-ceiling hypothesis, since it never read the template."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_28_flowchart_model_ladder_lift_skill_vs_capability_defect", "label": "Skill defect vs capability defect classification", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-28-flowchart-model-ladder-lift.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each lost criterion is labelled from the diff and trajectory: instruction missing/buried/ambiguous is fixable through whetstone; anything wording cannot reach is discarded and recorded as floor."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_28_flowchart_model_ladder_lift_harbor_wrong_pilot_skill", "label": "Harbor's marginal value is highest where the local loop is weakest", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-28-flowchart-model-ladder-lift.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "flowchart was the wrong skill to pilot Harbor on precisely because it is the best-instrumented skill in the repo \u2014 5 train / 4 val scored tasks, a held-out runner, a green floor. Harbor added a slow behavioural layer on top of a fast one that already worked. Revisit for a skill with no local scored surface, or when cross-model capability-floor data is wanted deliberately."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_28_flowchart_model_ladder_lift_acceptance_check_must_be_red", "label": "Prove every acceptanceCheck is RED before the whetstone run", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-28-flowchart-model-ladder-lift.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A check that is already green fixes nothing and will be kept spuriously by whetstone's keep-rule."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_28_flowchart_model_ladder_lift_wire_validator_into_verify", "label": "Backlog item: wire-output-validator-into-verify", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-28-flowchart-model-ladder-lift.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SKILL.md's verify step lists eyeball checks only and invokes nothing runnable, so every recorded Harbor run scored validator_passes: 0; feedback/plan-deck.jsonl filed the identical complaint against a sibling skill."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_28_flowchart_model_ladder_lift_harbor_tasks_drift_gate", "label": ".harbor/tasks drift gate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-28-flowchart-model-ladder-lift.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A tracked-but-derived mirror left unguarded when 13fae03 deleted the previous check; the CI step rebuilds and fails on drift."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_plans_2026_07_28_flowchart_model_ladder_lift_plan", "target": "readme_flowchart", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-28-flowchart-model-ladder-lift.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_plans_2026_07_28_flowchart_model_ladder_lift_plan", "target": "contributing_tier3_harbor", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-28-flowchart-model-ladder-lift.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"